   "id": 674117,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The US Census gathers and disseminates detailed big data about US residents. Visit <a href=\"https://openstax.org/r/datacensus\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Explore Census Data</a> and type your hometown into the search box. The results will include maps, web pages mentioning your hometown, and tables of information gathered by the decennial census as well as the American Community Survey. What method was used to collect this data? Do these tables represent probability or nonprobability samples? Why might these tables be important informational sources for marketers? Check out the table reporting age and sex. What is the median age? Does this statistic surprise you?",
